    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d164">

                <pb facs="0227" n="111" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg111"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/794.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American Ambassador
                        to Russia.</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d164-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 11, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The financial groups of France, Germany, Great Britain, and the United States,
                    with the sanction of their Governments, have agreed <pb facs="0228" n="112"
                        xml:id="pg112"/> to make an advance to meet the immediate needs of the
                    provisional government of united China. The groups are willing to concede equal
                    participation to Russia and Japan. You will cooperate with your British, French,
                    and German colleagues by informing the Minister, for Foreign Affairs that this
                    Government has approved the transaction on the condition that full and equal
                    participation be offered to Russia and Japan and would suggest that, if
                    agreeable to the Imperial Russian Government, a financial group or agency be
                    designated by that Government with which the groups of the other nationalities
                    may arrange the necessary details of this and future loans.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d164-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d164-f1-content">
                <p>Mutatis mutandis to American Embassy at Tokyo.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
